{
  "body_human_readable": "### \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" by the Numbers: Budget and Box Office\n\nThe 2005 film adaptation of Douglas Adams' beloved science fiction classic, \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy,\" was brought to the big screen with a production budget of approximately $45\u201350 million. The movie, directed by Garth Jennings, went on to achieve a worldwide gross of about $104.5 million at the box office.\n\nThe film, which stars Martin Freeman as the bewildered earthling Arthur Dent, Sam Rockwell as the two-headed galactic president Zaphod Beeblebrox, and Mos Def as the interstellar researcher Ford Prefect, was released in the United States on April 29, 2005. It garnered a variety of reviews but ultimately doubled its production budget in worldwide ticket sales. The movie's domestic gross was $51 million, with an international box office of $51.7 million. In its opening weekend in the U.S., the film topped the box office, earning an estimated $21.1 million.",
